WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.041 --> 00:00:16.724
Saturday morning, Katie and her mom walked to Pinker's Drugstore.

2
00:00:17.865 --> 00:00:21.008
Katie was wearing her captain cap and carrying Mr.

3
00:00:21.048 --> 00:00:21.968
Higgins' list.

4
00:00:23.069 --> 00:00:27.933
They went up and down the aisles, looking for the items they needed for the tornado shelter.

5
00:00:27.953 --> 00:00:31.196
"First aid cream," said Katie.

6
00:00:32.648 --> 00:00:33.108
"Got it!"

7
00:00:33.489 --> 00:00:36.271
said Mom, putting the tube in her shopping basket.

8
00:00:36.291 --> 00:00:39.913
"Bandages and tape," said Katie.

9
00:00:39.933 --> 00:00:42.355
"Bandages and tape!"

10
00:00:42.895 --> 00:00:43.476
said Mom.

11
00:00:44.516 --> 00:00:45.717
Katie looked at her list.

12
00:00:45.737 --> 00:00:48.259
"One more thing," she said.

13
00:00:48.279 --> 00:00:50.741
"We need a box to put everything in."

14
00:00:52.302 --> 00:00:54.303
Mom reached up to a high shelf.

15
00:00:54.904 --> 00:00:56.985
"Here's one that's the perfect size!"

16
00:00:57.485 --> 00:00:58.266
she exclaimed.

17
00:00:58.286 --> 00:01:01.108
"Great!" said Katie.

18
00:01:02.272 --> 00:01:03.412
"Great teamwork!"

19
00:01:03.852 --> 00:01:04.473
said Mom.

20
00:01:04.493 --> 00:01:07.834
"Good morning, Debra.

21
00:01:08.174 --> 00:01:09.994
Hello, Katie," said Mrs.

22
00:01:10.074 --> 00:01:11.254
Pinker at the checkout.

23
00:01:11.274 --> 00:01:13.775
"What have you got here?"

24
00:01:13.795 --> 00:01:18.656
"Katie and I are making a first aid kit," Mom explained.

25
00:01:18.677 --> 00:01:23.138
"We're getting ready for tornado season," said Katie.

26
00:01:23.158 --> 00:01:26.599
"I hope the Pinker family is prepared."

27
00:01:28.059 --> 00:01:31.200
Mrs. Pinker laughed and put their things in Mom's bag.

28
00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:36.841
As Katie and her mom stepped out of the drugstore, they heard a familiar voice.

29
00:01:38.082 --> 00:01:39.782
"Katie! Aunt Debra!"

30
00:01:40.843 --> 00:01:42.383
Katie looked across the street.

31
00:01:42.403 --> 00:01:44.644
"It's Luke," she said.

32
00:01:46.224 --> 00:01:51.386
Luke was sitting at a table in front of Aunt Sally's coffee shop, Fried Pie Heaven.

33
00:01:52.506 --> 00:02:01.825
He had taped a sign to the shop window: LIVE BAIT ONE DOZEN WET WORMS $1.00 Luke reached

34
00:02:01.885 --> 00:02:05.427
into a big tub of ice and held up a plastic cup.

35
00:02:05.447 --> 00:02:08.730
"Would you like some worms?"

36
00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:09.790
he asked with a grin.

37
00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:12.812
"Sorry," said Katie.

38
00:02:12.833 --> 00:02:14.314
"We already ate.

39
00:02:14.874 --> 00:02:17.656
HA!" She looked into the tub.

40
00:02:17.676 --> 00:02:20.518
"I hope you have enough," she said.

41
00:02:20.538 --> 00:02:24.681
"I don't have time for the bait business right now.

42
00:02:25.902 --> 00:02:28.724
I'm captain of the Donovan Tornado Safety Team."

43
00:02:29.912 --> 00:02:34.594
"Uh-oh, I forgot all about that," said Luke with a frown.

44
00:02:34.614 --> 00:02:38.195
"So you're not helping me dig worms anymore?"

45
00:02:39.436 --> 00:02:43.017
Just then Aunt Sally pushed open the door of the coffee shop.

46
00:02:44.138 --> 00:02:47.759
The scent of pie and fresh coffee filled the air outside.

47
00:02:47.779 --> 00:02:49.820
"Good morning!"

48
00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:51.121
she exclaimed.

49
00:02:51.741 --> 00:02:53.341
Aunt Sally was Mom's sister.

50
00:02:53.361 --> 00:02:59.284
"Mr. Higgins told our class to get our families ready for tornado season.

51
00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.621
Luke forgot," tattled Katie.

52
00:03:03.782 --> 00:03:09.684
Aunt Sally laughed as she brushed the flour from her apron and said, "I guess if a tornado

53
00:03:09.744 --> 00:03:11.425
comes, we'll just blow away!"

54
00:03:13.346 --> 00:03:14.846
Mom and Luke laughed too.

55
00:03:15.266 --> 00:03:17.107
Katie frowned and shook her head.

56
00:03:18.468 --> 00:03:21.849
She was the only one who seemed to be taking this seriously.

57
00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:28.472
Meanwhile Joy and Dad were on the slope above the Donovan pond looking at trees.

58
00:03:29.692 --> 00:03:31.813
They had just stopped under two elms.

59
00:03:33.274 --> 00:03:35.776
"These two trees might work," said Dad.

60
00:03:35.796 --> 00:03:37.957
"Let's see how far apart they are."

61
00:03:39.058 --> 00:03:41.219
He took a tape measure from his tool belt.

62
00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:46.102
"Here, hold your end of the tape on this tree," he said to Joy.

63
00:03:47.223 --> 00:03:50.525
Then he walked to the other tree, pulling the tape as he went.

64
00:03:50.545 --> 00:03:54.007
"One meter and twenty centimeters.

65
00:03:54.507 --> 00:03:55.828
Perfect," he said.

66
00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:00.882
"And this is a perfect spot for a tree house," said Joy.

67
00:04:00.902 --> 00:04:06.984
"From here, we can see the pond, the house, the chicken coop—everything!"

68
00:04:07.004 --> 00:04:11.366
"The two trees will hold up the back of the tree house," he said.

69
00:04:11.386 --> 00:04:14.347
"And we'll use two posts to hold up the front."

70
00:04:16.008 --> 00:04:20.069
Joy turned toward the house and saw Katie and Magoo racing up the hill.

71
00:04:20.089 --> 00:04:23.330
"Katie and Mom are back," she said.

72
00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:26.952
"I saw you from the road," called Katie.

73
00:04:27.456 --> 00:04:29.377
"Are you going to build the tree house here?"

74
00:04:29.397 --> 00:04:32.559
"Isn't this a perfect spot?"

75
00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:33.679
said Joy.

76
00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:35.761
Katie nodded.

77
00:04:35.781 --> 00:04:38.222
"It's excellent," she said.

78
00:04:38.242 --> 00:04:43.024
"I'll be able to watch the storm clouds roll in from the southwest.

79
00:04:44.105 --> 00:04:46.406
That's where tornadoes come from, you know."

80
00:04:47.567 --> 00:04:49.908
She looked up into the clear blue sky.

81
00:04:49.928 --> 00:04:54.931
"Good work, team," she said and ran back down the hill.

82
00:04:54.951 --> 00:04:58.163
"We better get busy," said Dad.

83
00:04:58.183 --> 00:05:00.611
"That's right, partner!"

84
00:05:01.112 --> 00:05:01.755
said Joy.
